<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40381" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rancĭdŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.
				dim.</i> [rancidus] (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>stinking</i>, <i>rank</i>, <i>rancid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opsonia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 135</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>disgusting</i>, <i>loathsome</i>, <i>offensive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rancidulum quiddam locutus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 33</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 34, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
